    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="AiEvaluationDefinition">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an agent evaluation, including subject metadata and a set of test cases. In Metadata API, you can create test definitions, including specifying inputs and expected outcomes, and deploy them to different orgs. In Connect API, you can execute test scenarios, poll for results, and retrieve test outcomes. This type extends the Metadata metadata type and inherits its fullName field. For more information on testing agents, see the Testing API Developer Guide.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_aievaluationdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The purpose of the test.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The API name of the test. Can contain only underscores and alphanumeric characters and must be unique in your org. It must begin with a letter, not include spaces, not end with an underscore, and not contain two consecutive underscores.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="subjectName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A unique identifier for the agent being tested. Make sure that this identifier matches the API name of the agent, which you can find on the agent details page in Setup.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="subjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The type of subject being tested. The only currently supported value is AGENT.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="subjectVersion" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The agent version to test. If not provided, the latest active version is used by default. You can find the version in the BotVersion metadata type.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="testCase" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of test cases.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="AiEvaluationExpectation">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the expected outcome for a test case.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_aievaluationdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="expectedValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The expected outcome of the test. The format of this field depends on the value of the name field. The expected outcome is compared against the response generated when you run the test using Connect REST API</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="label" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>An optional label for an expectation. Typically added when using the same custom expectation name multiple times in a test case. If provided, this label appears in the test results; otherwise, the expectation name appears.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The expectation name. Valid values are: topic_sequence_match: The expectedValue field value is a string representing the topic that the agent is expected to use, such as OOTBSingleRecordSummary. For a list of agent topics, see Standard Agent Topic Reference in Salesforce Help. action_sequence_match: The expectedValue field value is a string[] representing a list of actions that you expect the artifact to take during the test, such as [&apos;IdentifyRecordByName&apos;, &apos;action2&apos;]. For a list of agent actions, see Standard Agent Action Reference in Salesforce Help. This option was previously called action_sequence_match. bot_response_rating: The expectedValue field value is a string representing the expected response generated by the artifact, such as Summarization of the Global Media account. coherence: A generated answer is coherent if it’s easy to understand and has no grammatical errors. If you use this quality check, you don&apos;t need an expectedValue field value. completeness: A generated answer is complete if it includes all the essential information. If you use this quality check, you don&apos;t need an expectedValue field value. conciseness: A generated answer is concise if it&apos;s brief but comprehensive. Shorter is better. If you use this quality check, you don&apos;t need an expectedValue field value. output_latency_milliseconds: Latency in milliseconds from sending a request until a response is received. If you use this quality check, you don&apos;t need an expectedValue field value. string_comparison: A custom evaluation criteria that tests a response for a specified string value. numeric_comparison: A custom evaluation criteria that tests a response for a specified numeric value.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="parameter" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required for custom test criteria. An array of parameters for the specific custom criteria defined by expectation.name. This field replaces expectedValue for custom test criteria.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="AiEvaluationTestCase">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a test case.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_aievaluationdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="expectation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The criteria used to test the artifact&apos;s responses.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="inputs" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The specific input provided to the artifact being tested.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="number" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The unique number for the test case. If not provided, the value is automatically calculated.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="AiEvaluationTestCaseCritParam">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Defines a criterion parameter for expectations, including name, value, and whether it references another value. Available in API version 64.0 and later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_aievaluationdefinition.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="isReference" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>If true, indicates that value is a JSONPath expression referencing runtime data from the generatedData object returned by the Get Test Results resource. If true, the value must be a JSONPath string. The default value is false.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="name" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required for custom evaluation criteria. The name of the parameter required by the evaluation. Valid values are: operator—type of comparison; actual—runtime value to evaluate; expected—target value to compare against. For operator, valid options include: equals: Checks if the actual value exactly matches the expected value (string or numeric). contains: Checks if the actual string contains the expected string. startswith: Checks if the actual string begins with the expected string. endswith: Checks if the actual string ends with the expected string. greater_than_or_equal: Checks if the numeric actual value is greater than or equal to the numeric expected value (&gt;=). greater_than: Checks if the numeric actual value is greater than the numeric expected value (&gt;). less_than: Checks if the numeric actual value is less than the numeric expected value (&lt;). less_than_or_equal: Checks if the numeric actual value is less than or equal to the numeric expected value (&lt;=).</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="value" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required for custom evaluation criteria. The value for the parameter. This field can be a literal value or a JSONPath expression if isReference is true. Typically, JSONPath expressions are used to dynamically retrieve actual parameters.</xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomHttpHeaders">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents a custom HTTP header used with OData 2.0 or OData 4.0 connectors. Available in API version 43.0 or later.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_externaldatasource.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A text description of the header field’s purpose.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="headerFieldName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Name of the header field. The name must contain at least one alphanumeric character or underscore. It can also include these characters: ! # $ % &amp; &apos; * + - . ^ _ ` | ~.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="headerFieldValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. A formula that resolves to the value for the header. The values in the formula must evaluate to a string. If the formula resolves to null and an empty string, the header isn’t sent.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="isActive" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the custom HTTP header is available to use (true) or unavailable (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="CustomerDataPlatformSettings">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents an org&apos;s Data 360 settings.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_customerdataplatformsettings.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="enableCustomerDataPlatform" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether an org has Data 360 enabled (true) or not (false).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataConnector">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Represents the white-labeled metadata configuration for an external connector in Data 360.</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_dataconnector.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="attributes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="DataConnectorAttribute">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of configurable attributes for the data connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorAttribute[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="description" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The description of the data connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="errors" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="DataConnectorError">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of error messages or codes related to the connector’s behavior or configuration validation.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorError[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="features" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of features supported by the data connector. Values are: Override</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorFeature[] (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="icon" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A static resource in SVG format with dimensions of 100x100 pixels and a file size not exceeding 100 KB.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="licenseAgreement" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Text of the license agreement associated with the data connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The display label of the connector used in user interface (UI).</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ownerLocation" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A description or URL that specifies where the connector is maintained or hosted.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ownerLogo" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A static resource in SVG format with dimensions of 100x100 pixels and a file size not exceeding 100 KB.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="ownerName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The name of the organization that owns the connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="parentConnector" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The API name of the connector. For example, AwsS3, SNOWFLAKE, ICEBERG, and so on.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="releaseLevel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Indicates the connector’s lifecycle stage.Values are: BETA GA IN_DEV PILOT</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorReleaseLevel (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="supportEmail" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The support email address users can contact for help with the connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="supportMessage" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A support-related message or instruction displayed.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="supportPhone" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The support phone number users can call for help with the connector.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="translations" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of localized labels and descriptions to support multiple languages in the UI.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: LocalizedValue[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataConnectorAttribute">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Values are:</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_dataconnector.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
     <xsd:element name="capabilities" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of supported capabilities for the data connector.Values are: DataIn DataInDelete DataInHeader DataInIncremental DataInSelector DataInStructured DataInUnstructured DataOut Hidden UniqueGroup ZeroCopyIn</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorCapability[] (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="command" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The command string executed during data operations, such as import or sync.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="commandAttributes" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of attributes passed with the command.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="dataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. Specifies the type of data input expected.Values are: CHECKBOX COMBOBOX DATE DATETIME EMAIL IDP NAMED_CREDENTIAL NUMBER PASSWORD PASSWORD_FILE PRIVATE_NETWORK_ROUTE RADIO RADIO_BUTTONS TEXT TEXTAREA TIME TOGGLE</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorDataType (enumeration of type string)</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="defaultValue" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The default value assigned to the field if no user input is provided.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="editable" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field value can be modified by the user.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="externalName" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The unique name used to reference the connector externally, such as in API calls.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="masterLabel" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The label used for display in the UI.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="max" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The maximum allowable value or length for the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="min" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The minimum allowable value or length for the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="options" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="DataConnectorAttributeOpt">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of selectable options available for the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: DataConnectorAttributeOpt[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="order" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:int">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Required. The display order or evaluation order of the field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: int</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="pattern" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The validation pattern used to ensure input follows a defined format.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="placeholder" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The placeholder text displayed in the input field when empty.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="readonly" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field is read-only.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="required" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field must have a value.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="secure" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:boolean">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>Indicates whether the field contains sensitive data and should be masked.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: boolean</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="tooltip" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The tooltip text shown to users for additional guidance.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="translations" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:anyType">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>A list of localized labels and descriptions for use in different languages.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: LocalizedValue[]</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:element name="validationMessageError" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" type="xsd:string">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>The error message shown when input validation fails for this field.</xsd:documentation>
       <xsd:appinfo>Type: string</xsd:appinfo>
      </xsd:annotation>
     </xsd:element>
     <xsd:any minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded" processContents="lax"/>
    </xsd:choice>
   </xsd:extension>
  </xsd:complexContent>
 </xsd:complexType>
 <xsd:complexType name="DataConnectorAttributeOpt">
  <xsd:annotation>
   <xsd:documentation>Values are:</xsd:documentation>
   <xsd:appinfo>Documentation: https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_meta.meta/api_meta/meta_dataconnector.htm</xsd:appinfo>
  </xsd:annotation>
  <xsd:complexContent>
   <xsd:extension base="Metadata">
    <xsd:choice maxOccurs="unbounded">
